We have the source file solution.c and header state.h. The current implementation in solution.c has a setter that locks, sets lower, unlocks, yields, locks again, sets upper, unlocks. The getter reads lower without lock, yields, reads upper without lock. This allows inconsistent snapshots.

We need to fix so that both setter and getter access both fields under a single mutex lock. Also remove unnecessary sched_yield calls (they are not required for correctness and may cause delays). The requirement is to ensure atomic snapshot.

